CFG198 -- MUSE-DARK per galaxy: a0(z) at R_e from III's own DC14 products (route i), and whether III's rise survives
swapping the DC14-fitted disc mass for the SED stellar mass + main-sequence H2 (route ii, primary) or SED stars only
(route iii).  Frozen criteria: FROZEN_CRITERIA.md in this directory (d5a73127b), committed before any number.
kappa = 1/2 FITTED, NOT DERIVED.  Nothing here is graded as support for the framework.

Data: data_assembly/musedark_catalogues/musedark_numeric.csv (data chat, be78f2054 / f17dae96c); definitions as read, marked.

======================================================================================================================
CONTROLS
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] C1 exponential disc: peak at R/Rd in [2.1, 2.3] with v^2max Rd/(GM) = 0.3877 +- 0.001; Keplerian at 50 Rd within 0.5%
         peak R/Rd = 2.1500, v^2max Rd/GM = 0.38705; v^2 R/GM at 50 Rd = 1.00181
  [PASS] C2 kernel round trip nu(y*(D)) = D to 1e-9 for D in [1.06, 100] (nu_mono and nu_RAR)
         max rel error {'nu_mono': 1.199040866595169e-14, 'nu_RAR': 1.1102230246251565e-14}

======================================================================================================================
DATA AND SAMPLE
======================================================================================================================
  rows 126; with all needed columns 124; bulge galaxies set aside 14; disc-only 110; 0 < fDM_at_Re < 1: 109
  MUTATE=1: log M_fit -> log M_fit - 0.4 (z - 0.863) (an injected fitted-mass drift at fixed g_obs)

======================================================================================================================
C3 ROUTE IDENTITY
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] C3 route identity: with M*_SED := M_fit and mu_mol := 0, route (ii) equals route (i) (every a0 ratio 1 to 1e-12)
         max |ratio - 1| = 0.00e+00 over 106 galaxies

